                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_03\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit removes the properties `OUTPUT_ENCODING` (\"html.outputEncoding\") and `SOURCE_ENCODING` (\"html.sourceEncoding\") \u2014 explicitly labeled in the code as \"addition parameters by terry\" \u2014 and restores the original `OUT_ENCODING`/`IN_ENCODING` scheme (adding a new `IN_ENCODING` property alongside the pre-existing `OUT_ENCODING`). It reverts all call sites (html/txt/xml ReportGenerator classes) from `getOutputEncoding()`/`getSourceEncoding()` back to `getOutEncoding()`/`getInEncoding()`.\n\nSearching the candidates for these exact symbols shows:\n- candidate_01: contains only `OUT_ENCODING` (the original, correct scheme) \u2014 bug not yet present.\n- candidate_02: no encoding-related changes.\n- candidate_03: introduces `OUTPUT_ENCODING`/`SOURCE_ENCODING` for the first time, with the literal comment \"addition parameters by terry\", adds `setOutputEncoding`/`setSourceEncoding` to `ParsedProperties`, and switches `ReportProperties.parse()` to read from these new properties instead of `OUT_ENCODING`. It also changes source-file reading in the HTML report generator from `FileReader` (platform default encoding) to an explicit `InputStreamReader` using the new `getSourceEncoding()`, and switches multiple `getOutEncoding()` call sites to `getOutputEncoding()`.\n- candidate_04: unrelated change (renames a directory constant from \"_files\" to \"files\").\n- candidate_05: reverts back to `OUT_ENCODING`/`IN_ENCODING` (content matching the eventual fix), meaning the buggy scheme introduced in candidate_03 was still present up through candidate_04.\n\nBecause candidate_03 is the first commit to introduce the `OUTPUT_ENCODING`/`SOURCE_ENCODING` properties (the exact code structure and naming that the fix commit removes), it is the bug-introducing commit. The unrelated candidate_04 confirms the bug persisted until directly addressed.\n"
